# The `server` service builds with `context: .` (see docker-compose.yml), so
# THIS file is the one Docker reads — server/.dockerignore is never consulted
# for that build, because Docker only reads .dockerignore from the context root.
#
# server/Dockerfile COPYs nothing: the source arrives through the ./server:/app
# bind mount, so none of this needs to be sent as build context anyway.
#
# server/target matters most. The container's `cargo build` runs as root
# against that bind mount, so it leaves root-owned 0600 files on the host that
# the context walker cannot read:
#   checking context: no permission to read from '.../incremental/...lock'
# It is also ~2 GB, which the daemon would otherwise scan on every build.

server/target
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
.git
*.pdf
